cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use these data or maps, please cite this repository and also the
  original source of each series (Calvo; Lupu and Stokes; Cantón; DINE; CNE)
  and the department geometry (Rodríguez and De Grande, CEUR-CONICET,
  CC BY 2.5 AR). Each atlas's LEEME file lists its sources.
type: dataset
title: "Atlas electorales de Argentina 1904-2025"
authors:
  - family-names: "Rodríguez Paolini"
    given-names: "Juan Cruz"
repository-code: "https://github.com/azha2005/257arg"
url: "https://azha2005.github.io/257arg/"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Department-level results and atlases for Argentine elections from 1904 to
  2025 (80+ elections: president, national deputies, runoffs, primaries and
  constituent assemblies), AMBA results by census tract 2003-2025,
  ecological-inference estimates of vote transfers (Python port of
  E. Calvo's method) and Wikimedia Commons packages. No Argentine public
  body publishes this compilation. Code is licensed under MIT; the project's
  own data, maps and texts under CC BY 4.0 (see LICENSE-DATA.md).
  Third-party data, geometry and logos keep their own terms.
keywords:
  - Argentina
  - elections
  - electoral geography
  - historical GIS
  - ecological inference
  - maps
